WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.490
The children followed Julio out of the church and into the street.

2
00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:17.143
The streets of Palos were busy with people carrying goods.

3
00:00:17.144 --> 00:00:22.915
They were carrying supplies in their hands, in wagons, and on animals.

4
00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:28.260
Everyone was heading in the same direction: to the docks.

5
00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:32.247
Julio led the children in that direction as well.

6
00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:37.001
Mandy could smell the ocean before she saw it.

7
00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:40.871
"Mandy, look!" cried Vinnie.

8
00:00:40.872 --> 00:00:44.078
At the end of the street was the harbor.

9
00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:48.185
Vinnie pointed to three ships tied up at the pier.

10
00:00:48.186 --> 00:00:51.394
One was bigger than the other two.

11
00:00:51.395 --> 00:00:54.963
"The biggest one is—," began Julio.

12
00:00:54.964 --> 00:00:57.458
"The Santa Maria.

13
00:00:57.459 --> 00:01:02.260
And the others are the Pinta and Niña," said Vinnie.

14
00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:04.891
Julio looked impressed.

15
00:01:04.892 --> 00:01:09.816
"You'd better return that book to Columbus," Julio said to Mandy.

16
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:12.327
"He won't sail without it."

17
00:01:12.328 --> 00:01:16.398
"Where can I find him?" asked Mandy.

18
00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:21.158
"Aboard the Santa Maria, of course," replied Julio.

19
00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:25.005
"Can you take us there?" said Mandy.

20
00:01:25.006 --> 00:01:30.370
"Sure, come on," Julio said, waving his hand.

21
00:01:30.371 --> 00:01:33.877
They walked down the street to the pier.

22
00:01:33.878 --> 00:01:36.519
The harbor was busy.

23
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:41.221
Men were loading all kinds of equipment onto the ships.

24
00:01:41.222 --> 00:01:44.469
Seagulls circled above the waves.

25
00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:48.707
Along the way, they asked Julio more questions.

26
00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:54.253
"Why are the sailors afraid of sailing west?" Mandy asked.

27
00:01:54.254 --> 00:01:57.716
Julio took a breath.

28
00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.357
He was still nervous about the trip.

29
00:02:01.358 --> 00:02:05.093
"It is said that sea monsters live in those waters.

30
00:02:05.094 --> 00:02:11.447
Even if you somehow sail past them, well . . . ," Julio paused.

31
00:02:11.448 --> 00:02:14.376
"The ocean ends at some point.

32
00:02:14.377 --> 00:02:18.508
Then what happens?"

33
00:02:18.509 --> 00:02:22.622
"Oh, don't worry. The world is round.

34
00:02:22.623 --> 00:02:26.895
Your ship won't fall," laughed Vinnie.

35
00:02:26.896 --> 00:02:31.737
"How do you know what is out there?" Julio said angrily.

36
00:02:31.738 --> 00:02:36.059
"I bet you haven't been on an adventure in your life!"

37
00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.605
Vinnie and Mandy smiled at each other and thought of their photo trips.

38
00:02:41.606 --> 00:02:45.021
"Julio!" someone called.

39
00:02:45.022 --> 00:02:48.642
A middle-aged woman approached them.

40
00:02:48.643 --> 00:02:51.687
She was carrying a wool blanket.

41
00:02:51.688 --> 00:02:58.451
"Señora Molina! What a pleasant surprise!" Julio cried happily.

42
00:02:58.452 --> 00:03:01.819
He introduced the children to her.

43
00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.855
"Señora Molina owns a wool shop.

44
00:03:04.856 --> 00:03:09.587
Her wool is the softest and warmest in all of Spain."

45
00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.507
"Here, take this,"

46
00:03:11.508 --> 00:03:16.026
said Señora Molina, handing the blanket to Julio.

47
00:03:16.027 --> 00:03:19.338
"This will keep you warm on cold nights."

48
00:03:19.339 --> 00:03:23.464
"Thank you so much," Julio said.

49
00:03:23.465 --> 00:03:25.651
He hugged her.

50
00:03:25.652 --> 00:03:30.779
"Be careful, Julio," she whispered, wiping her eyes.

51
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:37.621
Julio waved good-bye, then he and Mandy and Vinnie continued onto the pier.

52
00:03:37.622 --> 00:03:40.869
"One day I will make Spanish wool famous,"

53
00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.534
said Julio, holding the soft blanket close to him.

54
00:03:45.535 --> 00:03:48.356
"How?" asked Vinnie.

55
00:03:48.357 --> 00:03:56.071
"When I have my own ship, I will sell wool at every port on earth," Julio said proudly.

56
00:03:56.072 --> 00:04:01.963
"Maybe you'll become an explorer like Columbus," said Mandy.

57
00:04:01.964 --> 00:04:05.938
"Who wants to be like him?" replied Julio.

58
00:04:05.939 --> 00:04:09.825
"He's a dreamer with some crazy ideas."

59
00:04:09.826 --> 00:04:14.014
"But look at him now!" exclaimed Mandy.

60
00:04:14.015 --> 00:04:17.966
"Look at what?" Julio laughed.

61
00:04:17.967 --> 00:04:27.697
"He hasn't discovered anything yet!"
